---
/*
 * cbf-libmvp-cost-table — the vendor Line Item Budget (LIB) entry grid, v1.
 * The LIB of a CBFish contract at /lib-mvp, and of each subcontract at
 * /lib-mvp/subcontract/<sheet>.
 *
 * A FORK of src/components/lib-entry/cbf-lib-cost-table.astro (the long-term
 * exploration behind /lib-entry, left untouched), cut to docs/lib-mvp-scope.md
 * and read against src/data/lib-mvp.mjs. What v1 cut is gone from the markup,
 * not hidden: trips, published-rate claims, GSA columns, work-element
 * allocation, accounting codes, import and copy, the personnel split, rate
 * steps, capitalization-threshold filing and drag-to-reorder.
 *
 * ── THE DESIGN CLAIM ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * A LIB is a web of cross-line dependencies, not a list of independent rows:
 * fringe is a percentage of a salary line, a cell phone's months may FOLLOW a
 * position, indirect is a percentage of whatever its base reaches. A grid holds
 * that web — the salary line and everything that follows it are on screen at
 * once — so there is no add-line modal: "Add line" appends an editable row
 * inline, of the kind the vendor picked.
 *
 * ── EVERY CATEGORY CAPTIONS ITS OWN COLUMNS ─────────────────────────────────
 * No global <thead>. "Quantity" is months in Personnel, rooms × nights in a
 * lodging line and nothing at all in Fringe, so each of the nine categories
 * emits its own caption row (`columns` in src/data/lib-mvp.mjs). Only Amount
 * and the row action keep one name, because the money column has to line up
 * with the subtotals and the foot.
 *
 * ── THE THREE LINE SHAPES — the ROW decides its cells ───────────────────────
 *   qty-rate     identity · quantity (+ a second quantity where the unit has
 *                one) · cost per unit. The vendor types the rate. Travel is one
 *                of these: a kind, a typed destination, count × duration × rate.
 *   pct-of-base  fringe ONLY, generated one per salary line. Nothing to type:
 *                the row says what it is a percentage of and where to edit it.
 *   lump         label · one amount · a description (gated). A subcontract
 *                line is a lump whose amount is its child LIB's total.
 * A collapsed cell is a spanned cell, never a dead input.
 *
 * ── "WHAT IS THIS LINE" IS A PICKER, NOT PROSE ──────────────────────────────
 * Plain dropdowns over fixed lists: travel kind, vehicle kind + vehicle type,
 * meeting kind, other kind, a position's time unit. The kind fixes the units;
 * a vehicle TYPE prefills the GSA Fleet rate as an editable default
 * (prefillVehicleRate never overwrites a number the vendor typed).
 *
 * ── LINKED QUANTITIES — one hop, to a position ──────────────────────────────
 * From the row menu: follow a position's time, stop following ("Use my own
 * quantity", which freezes the value), or follow it again. Editing the
 * position flashes every row that just moved (`dependentsOf`).
 *
 * ── ARITHMETIC IS NEVER DONE HERE ───────────────────────────────────────────
 * Every amount, subtotal and total comes from `priceLines(lines, cfg)`, re-run
 * in full after every edit, so a dependent line cannot silently disagree with
 * its base.
 *
 * ── WHO MAY TOUCH WHAT ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * The vendor edits only while `vendorCanEdit(review)` (draft / returned); while
 * the budget is with the COR, or once it is approved, the vendor reads the
 * same facts the COR does, under a short notice. The COR marks lines only
 * while `corCanMark(review)` (in review). Both renderings are in the markup;
 * the read lens is the document's `data-cbf-role="cor"` (set before paint) or
 * this grid's own `data-lens="read"`.
 *
 * ── AUTOSAVE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * There is no backend, so a committed edit (a field's change on blur, a pick,
 * a menu action) writes this budget's working lines to sessionStorage
 * (`cbf-libmvp-lines:<budget>`, see src/lib/lib-mvp-view.ts) and shows
 * "Saved". The main budget reads every stored child sheet on mount, so a
 * child LIB's total reaches its subcontract line on the parent page.
 *
 * ── EVENT CONTRACT (all on `document`, names from EVENTS in lib-mvp.mjs) ────
 * DISPATCH EVENTS.totals — on mount and after EVERY recompute. The budget's
 *   lines are written to storage BEFORE it fires.
 *   detail: { budget, total, direct, indirect, indirectBase, remaining,
 *             pctOfValue, checks, advisories, lines }
 *   budget     'main' or the subcontract sheet id
 *   checks     submitChecksFor(lines, cfg, { openRequired, budgetId })
 *   advisories advisoriesFor(lines, cfg)
 * LISTEN EVENTS.indirect     detail: { config: { rateId } } — reprice, re-fire.
 * LISTEN EVENTS.review       detail: { review } — repaint marks and
 *   permissions, recompute the checks, re-fire totals.
 * LISTEN EVENTS.focusLine    detail: { lineId, budget? } — open the section,
 *   scroll to and flash the row. A line on another budget is ignored; a page
 *   links to it instead (`/lib-mvp/subcontract/<sheet>#<lineId>`), which the
 *   grid honors on mount.
 * LISTEN cbf-role:change     repaint the lens.
 * When the grid changes a mark (setFlag / removeFlag / setAddressed) it calls
 *   saveReview + fireReview.
 * NAVIGATES to /lib-mvp/subcontract/<sheet> from a subcontract row.
 *
 * bcn-lego-checked: the house rule points data tables at AG Grid, but that rule
 * governs SCANNABLE data grids with search / filter / download chrome. This is an
 * ENTRY FORM — a live control and its own validation state in most cells, with
 * per-row shape branching and colspan collapse — so a semantic <table> carrying
 * esa-* controls is both correct and far lighter. Same call the /lib-entry grid,
 * cbf-baselines-table and cbf-lib-pi-documents already made; the ecology catalog
 * was re-checked and has no table/grid lego. Everything that ISN'T the grid is a
 * lego: entry cells = esa-text-field, pickers = esa-select, add-line and row
 * menus = esa-dropdown-menu, the COR mark editor = esa-popover + esa-radio-group
 * + esa-textarea, "addressed" = esa-checkbox, notices = esa-alert-box, the
 * first-run state = esa-empty-state, validation = esa-field-error, verdicts =
 * esa-badge, the fringe setting = esa-dialog. The "Saved" indicator is an
 * esa-icon beside one line of text — no lego carries a passive save status.
 * Beacon is not cloned on this machine.
 */
import EsaButton from '@esa/ecology/esa-button.astro';
import EsaBadge from '@esa/ecology/esa-badge.astro';
import EsaFieldError from '@esa/ecology/esa-field-error.astro';
import EsaIcon from '@esa/ecology/esa-icon.astro';
import EsaAlertBox from '@esa/ecology/esa-alert-box.astro';
import EsaEmptyState from '@esa/ecology/esa-empty-state.astro';
import {
  SHAPES,
  budgetFor,
  priceLines,
  effectiveQty,
  baseAmountFor,
  baseLabelFor,
  contract,
  timeUnit,
  isSalaryLine,
  travelKind,
  vehicleKind,
  vehicleTypeLabel,
  meetingKind,
  otherKind,
  ENTRY_COLUMNS,
  hasFringeCell,
  rateSpan,
  blockOf,
  usd,
  pct,
  qtyFmt,
} from '../../data/lib-mvp.mjs';
import {
  SEVERITIES,
  severityMeta,
  reasonLabel,
  seedReview,
  flagFor,
  isAddressed,
  vendorCanEdit,
  openRequiredFlags,
} from '../../data/lib-mvp-review.mjs';
import * as V from '../../lib/lib-mvp-view';

interface Props {
  /**
   * Which budget to render: 'main' (the contract's LIB) or a subcontract sheet
   * id, whose child LIB has the same sections less Subcontracts, and no
   * indirect. See budgetFor / activateBudget in src/data/lib-mvp.mjs.
   */
  budget?: string;
  /** Section heading above the grid. Pass null to let the page own the heading. */
  heading?: string | null;
  /** One line of context under the heading. Pass null to omit. */
  lede?: string | null;
}
const {
  budget = 'main',
  heading = 'Line item budget',
  lede = `${contract.number} · ${contract.fiscalYear} · ${contract.periodStart}–${contract.periodEnd}`,
} = Astro.props;

const B: any = budgetFor(budget);
const isSub = B.kind === 'subcontract';
const categories: any[] = B.categories;
const cfg: any = B.cfg;
const lines: any[] = B.lines;
const priced = priceLines(lines, cfg);
const A = priced.amounts;
const amt = (id: string): number => A[id] ?? 0;
const t0 = priced.totals;

/* ── The COR's review layer ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Server-rendered from the seeded review, then kept live by the script. A mark
   renders inside the cost-line cell, under the line it disputes. Only this
   budget's marks — one review covers the parent and every child LIB. */
const review = seedReview();
const openRequired = openRequiredFlags(review);
const flagOf = (l: any) => {
  const f = flagFor(review, l.id);
  return f && (f.budget ?? 'main') === B.id ? f : null;
};

/* ── View derivations, bound to THIS scope's data ───────────────────────────
   The bodies live in src/lib/lib-mvp-view.ts; the client script binds the same
   ones to its live state, so the two scopes cannot drift. */
const displayLabel = (l: any) => V.displayLabel(l, lines);
const firstError = (l: any) => V.lineErrors(l, lines)[0] ?? '';

/* ── Grouping: a flat item list per category, so the row markup is written once
   whether or not the category has sub-blocks (only Supplies does). ── */
const linesIn = (catKey: string, blockKey?: string) =>
  lines.filter((l) => l.category === catKey && (blockKey ? l.block === blockKey : true));
const itemsFor = (cat: any): any[] =>
  cat.blocks
    ? cat.blocks.flatMap((b: any) => [
        { kind: 'block', block: b },
        ...linesIn(cat.key, b.key).map((line: any) => ({ kind: 'line', line })),
      ])
    : linesIn(cat.key).map((line: any) => ({ kind: 'line', line }));

/* ── Row templates, one per SHAPE ───────────────────────────────────────────
   An added line clones a real server-rendered row of its shape, so its esa-*
   legos and colspan collapse are byte-identical to the SSR ones. A budget may
   have no row of some shape (a new subcontract's LIB has none at all), so one
   blank row per shape renders in a hidden tbody the script takes and removes.
   The salary template also carries the fringe cell other qty-rate rows drop. */
const TEMPLATE_LINES = [
  { id: 'tpl-qty-rate', category: 'personnel-salary', shape: SHAPES.QTY_RATE, label: '', qty: 1, staff: 1, timeUnit: 'month', qtyUnit: 'months', rate: 0 },
  { id: 'tpl-pct-of-base', category: 'personnel-fringe', shape: SHAPES.PCT_OF_BASE, derived: true, base: { type: 'line', lineId: '' }, pct: 0 },
  { id: 'tpl-lump', category: 'other', shape: SHAPES.LUMP, label: '', amount: 0, desc: '' },
];
const groups: any[] = [
  ...categories.map((cat) => ({ cat, items: itemsFor(cat) })),
  { cat: null, items: TEMPLATE_LINES.map((line) => ({ kind: 'line', line })) },
];

/* The row-actions trigger is a vertical ellipsis. The hub's icon registry has
   none (logged in docs/hub-issues.md), so the Lucide paths go through esa-icon's
   own `paths` fallback, inside a chrome esa-button. */
const KEBAB_PATHS = '<circle cx="12" cy="12" r="1"/><circle cx="12" cy="5" r="1"/><circle cx="12" cy="19" r="1"/>';
---

<section class="cbf-lct stack" data-gap="md" data-lct data-libmvp-surface data-budget={B.id} data-budget-kind={B.kind}>
  <header class="repel" data-gap="sm">
    <span class="stack" data-gap="3xs">
      {heading && <h2 class="typography-heading-md">{heading}</h2>}
      {lede && <p class="cbf-lct__lede">{lede}</p>}
    </span>
    <span class="cluster" data-gap="xs">
      {/* Per-line autosave, made visible: a committed edit says it landed. */}
      <span class="cbf-lct__saved" role="status" aria-live="polite">
        <span class="cluster" data-gap="3xs" data-saved hidden>
          <EsaIcon name="check" size="sm" />
          <span>Saved</span>
        </span>
      </span>
      <span data-unfold-all><EsaButton size="sm" variant="ghost" icon="chevron-down">Expand all</EsaButton></span>
      <span data-fold-all><EsaButton size="sm" variant="ghost" icon="chevron-up">Collapse all</EsaButton></span>
    </span>
  </header>

  {/* ── Why the grid is read-only right now — one notice, for whoever is reading ── */}
  <div data-notice="in-review" hidden>
    <EsaAlertBox variant="info" title="With the BPA COR for review">
      You can’t edit the budget while it’s in review. It opens again if the COR returns it.
    </EsaAlertBox>
  </div>
  <div data-notice="approved" hidden>
    <EsaAlertBox variant="success" title="Approved and locked">
      Changes to this budget now go through a contract change.
    </EsaAlertBox>
  </div>
  <div data-notice="cor-wait" hidden>
    <EsaAlertBox variant="info" title="Not in review">
      You can mark lines once the vendor submits the budget.
    </EsaAlertBox>
  </div>

  {/* ── First run: a budget with nothing in it yet ── */}
  <div data-empty hidden>
    <EsaEmptyState title="No cost lines yet" description="Add a line to any section below." size="md" />
  </div>

  <!-- overflow stays visible at desktop on purpose: the esa-popover mark editor,
       the esa-select panels and the esa-dropdown-menu menus position absolutely
       and cannot escape a clipping ancestor. Narrow viewports fall back to
       horizontal scrolling and accept the clipping. -->
  <div class="cbf-lct__scroll">
    <table class="cbf-lct__table" aria-label="Line item budget cost lines">
      {groups.map((g: any) => (
        <tbody
          data-cat={g.cat?.key}
          data-collapsed={g.cat ? '' : undefined}
          data-tpl={g.cat ? undefined : ''}
          hidden={!g.cat}
        >
          {g.cat && (
            <>
              {/* ── Category head: name, count, subtotal, and the inline add ── */}
              <tr class="cbf-lct__cathead">
                <th scope="colgroup" colspan={ENTRY_COLUMNS}>
                  <span class="repel cbf-lct__cathead-row" data-gap="sm">
                    {/* Folding: folded, a section is one line — what it is, how
                        many lines, what it costs, and whether any needs a fix. */}
                    <span class="cluster" data-gap="2xs">
                      <span data-cat-toggle>
                        <EsaButton variant="chrome" size="xs" iconOnly icon="chevron-down" label={`Show or hide ${g.cat.label}`} aria-expanded="false" />
                      </span>
                      {g.cat.icon && (
                        <span class="cbf-lct__cat-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                          <EsaIcon name={g.cat.icon} paths={g.cat.iconPaths} size="sm" />
                        </span>
                      )}
                      <span class="cbf-lct__cat-label">{g.cat.label}</span>
                      <span class="cbf-lct__note" data-cat-count>
                        {(() => { const n = linesIn(g.cat.key).length; return n ? `${n} line${n === 1 ? '' : 's'}` : 'No lines'; })()}
                      </span>
                      <span data-cat-issues hidden>
                        <EsaBadge value="Needs attention" variant="warning" size="sm" />
                      </span>
                      {g.cat.key === 'personnel-salary' && (
                        <span data-fringe-badge hidden={!V.fringeBadge()}>
                          <EsaBadge value={V.fringeBadge() ?? ''} variant="info" size="sm" />
                        </span>
                      )}
                      {g.cat.note && (
                        <esa-popover position="right" trigger="click" offset="6">
                          <EsaButton size="xs" variant="ghost" icon="info" label={`Learn more about ${g.cat.label}`}>Learn more</EsaButton>
                          <div slot="content" class="cbf-lct__cat-note">{g.cat.note}</div>
                        </esa-popover>
                      )}
                    </span>
                    <span class="cbf-lct__cat-add" data-vendor-only>
                      {g.cat.derived ? (
                        /* A generated section has nothing to add TO — the cell
                           says where its lines come from instead. */
                        <span class="cbf-lct__note">Set fringe on the salary lines.</span>
                      ) : g.cat.shapes.length > 1 || g.cat.blocks || g.cat.kinds ? (
                        /* More than one kind (or sub-block): the add is a menu. */
                        <esa-dropdown-menu position="below-end" data-add-menu={g.cat.key}>
                          <EsaButton size="sm" variant="primary" appearance="outline" icon="plus">Add line</EsaButton>
                        </esa-dropdown-menu>
                      ) : (
                        <EsaButton size="sm" variant="primary" appearance="outline" icon="plus" data-add-line={`${g.cat.key}||${g.cat.shapes[0]}|`}>
                          Add line
                        </EsaButton>
                      )}
                    </span>
                  </span>
                </th>
                <td class="cbf-lct__cell cbf-lct__cell--num">
                  <strong class="cbf-lct__money" data-cat-total={g.cat.key}>{usd(priced.byCategory[g.cat.key] ?? 0)}</strong>
                </td>
                {/* The section's own menu — Personnel's default fringe rate is the
                    one section setting v1 keeps. */}
                <td class="cbf-lct__cell cbf-lct__cell--act">
                  {g.cat.key === 'personnel-salary' && (
                    <span data-vendor-only>
                      <esa-dropdown-menu position="below-end" data-cat-menu={g.cat.key}>
                        <EsaButton variant="chrome" size="sm" class="cbf-lct__kebab" aria-label={`Options for ${g.cat.label}`} title={`Options for ${g.cat.label}`}>
                          <EsaIcon name="ellipsis-vertical" paths={KEBAB_PATHS} size="sm" />
                        </EsaButton>
                      </esa-dropdown-menu>
                    </span>
                  )}
                </td>
              </tr>

              {/* ── This category's OWN column captions ── */}
              <tr class="cbf-lct__colhead">
                <th scope="col" class="cbf-lct__col-line">{g.cat.columns.line}</th>
                {g.cat.columns.span ? (
                  <th scope="col" class="cbf-lct__col-span" colspan={ENTRY_COLUMNS - 1}>{g.cat.columns.span}</th>
                ) : (
                  <>
                    <th scope="col" class="cbf-lct__col-qty">
                      {g.cat.columns.qty ?? <span class="cbf-lct__sr">This section has no quantity column</span>}
                    </th>
                    <th scope="col" class="cbf-lct__col-rate" colspan={g.cat.columns.fringe ? undefined : 2}>{g.cat.columns.rate}</th>
                    {g.cat.columns.fringe && <th scope="col" class="cbf-lct__col-fringe">{g.cat.columns.fringe}</th>}
                  </>
                )}
                <th scope="col" class="cbf-lct__col-num">Amount</th>
                <th scope="col" class="cbf-lct__col-act"><span class="cbf-lct__sr">Row actions</span></th>
              </tr>
            </>
          )}

          {g.items.map((item: any) =>
            item.kind === 'block' ? (
              /* ── Sub-block head with its own subtotal (Supplies only) ──
                 Which class an item lands in decides whether the indirect rate
                 reaches it and whether it becomes tracked property, so the
                 block states its rule. */
              <tr class="cbf-lct__blockhead" data-blockhead={item.block.key}>
                <th scope="rowgroup" colspan={ENTRY_COLUMNS}>
                  <span class="stack" data-gap="2xs">
                    <span class="cbf-lct__block-label">{item.block.label}</span>
                    {item.block.note && <span class="cbf-lct__note">{item.block.note}</span>}
                  </span>
                </th>
                <td class="cbf-lct__cell cbf-lct__cell--num">
                  <span class="cbf-lct__money" data-block-total={`${g.cat.key}:${item.block.key}`}>
                    {usd(priced.byBlock[`${g.cat.key}:${item.block.key}`] ?? 0)}
                  </span>
                </td>
                <td class="cbf-lct__cell cbf-lct__cell--act"></td>
              </tr>
            ) : (
              <tr
                data-line={item.line.id}
                data-shape={item.line.shape}
                data-cat={item.line.category}
                data-block={blockOf(item.line)}
                data-flag={V.rowFlag(item.line, lines)}
              >
                {/* ── 1. The line's IDENTITY — and the mark, if it carries one ──
                     Every identity control ships on every row and the ones this
                     category uses are revealed, which keeps a CLONED row correct
                     in whatever category it lands. */}
                <td class="cbf-lct__cell cbf-lct__cell--line">
                  <div class="stack" data-gap="2xs">
                    <span data-kind-pick="travel" hidden={item.line.category !== 'travel'}>
                      <esa-select class="cbf-lct__select" size="sm" data-travel-kind-select
                        placeholder={travelKind(item.line.travelKind)?.label ?? 'Pick a travel kind'}
                        aria-label={`Travel kind — ${displayLabel(item.line) || 'new line'}`}></esa-select>
                    </span>
                    <span data-kind-pick="vehicles" hidden={item.line.category !== 'vehicles'}>
                      <esa-select class="cbf-lct__select" size="sm" data-vehicle-kind-select
                        placeholder={vehicleKind(item.line.vehicleKind)?.label ?? 'Pick a vehicle cost'}
                        aria-label={`Vehicle cost — ${displayLabel(item.line) || 'new line'}`}></esa-select>
                    </span>
                    {/* The TYPE stays on the row: the COR checks the class against
                        the work, and it is what prefills the GSA rate. */}
                    <span data-vehicle-type hidden={!V.takesVehicleType(item.line)}>
                      <esa-select class="cbf-lct__select" size="sm" data-vehicle-type-select
                        placeholder={vehicleTypeLabel(item.line.vehicleType) || 'Pick the vehicle type'}
                        aria-label={`Vehicle type — ${displayLabel(item.line) || 'new line'}`}></esa-select>
                    </span>
                    <span data-kind-pick="meetings" hidden={item.line.category !== 'meetings'}>
                      <esa-select class="cbf-lct__select" size="sm" data-meeting-kind-select
                        placeholder={meetingKind(item.line.meetingKind)?.label ?? 'Pick a kind'}
                        aria-label={`Kind of training cost — ${displayLabel(item.line) || 'new line'}`}></esa-select>
                    </span>
                    <span data-kind-pick="other" hidden={!(item.line.category === 'other' && item.line.shape === SHAPES.QTY_RATE)}>
                      <esa-select class="cbf-lct__select" size="sm" data-other-kind-select
                        placeholder={otherKind(item.line.otherKind)?.label ?? 'Pick a kind'}
                        aria-label={`Kind of cost — ${displayLabel(item.line) || 'new line'}`}></esa-select>
                    </span>

                    {/* Typed name — a position title, an item, a subcontractor. */}
                    <span data-ident-label hidden={V.identOf(item.line) !== 'label'}>
                      <esa-text-field class="cbf-lct__field cbf-lct__field--label" size="sm" data-field="label"
                        value={item.line.label ?? ''}
                        placeholder={V.labelPlaceholderOf(item.line)}
                        aria-label={`Name — ${displayLabel(item.line) || 'new line'}`}></esa-text-field>
                    </span>

                    {/* Travel names where it goes as plain text — never looked up. */}
                    <span data-travel-dest hidden={item.line.category !== 'travel'}>
                      <esa-text-field class="cbf-lct__field cbf-lct__field--label" size="sm" data-field="destination"
                        value={item.line.destination ?? ''}
                        placeholder="Destination — a town, county or site"
                        aria-label={`Destination — ${displayLabel(item.line) || 'new line'}`}></esa-text-field>
                    </span>

                    {/* A lump says what it covers (gated); a vendor-defined travel
                        or vehicle line says what it is (its name). */}
                    <span data-desc hidden={!V.takesDesc(item.line)}>
                      <esa-text-field class="cbf-lct__field cbf-lct__field--label" size="sm" data-field="desc"
                        value={item.line.desc ?? ''}
                        placeholder={V.descPlaceholderOf(item.line)}
                        aria-label={`Description — ${displayLabel(item.line) || 'new line'}`}></esa-text-field>
                    </span>

                    {/* Fringe names itself after the position it follows. */}
                    <span class="cbf-lct__derived" data-cell="ident-derived" hidden={V.identOf(item.line) !== 'derived'}>
                      {displayLabel(item.line)}
                    </span>

                    {/* The read lens: the name and description as values. */}
                    <span class="cbf-lct__fact cbf-lct__fact--label" data-fact="label">{displayLabel(item.line) || 'Untitled line'}</span>
                    <span class="cbf-lct__fact cbf-lct__note" data-fact="desc" hidden={!V.isPlainLump(item.line) || !(item.line.desc ?? '').trim()}>
                      {item.line.desc ?? ''}
                    </span>

                    {/* Quiet, not a warning: a vendor-defined line is allowed. */}
                    <span data-vendor-badge hidden={!V.vendorDefined(item.line)}>
                      <EsaBadge value="Vendor-defined" variant="info" size="sm" />
                    </span>

                    {/* Inline validation — only the submit gates that read one line. */}
                    <span data-line-err hidden={!firstError(item.line)}>
                      <EsaFieldError message={firstError(item.line)} icon />
                    </span>

                    {/* ── The COR's mark, on the line it disputes ──
                        Visible as soon as it is made. The vendor ticks it
                        addressed here, beside the numbers it is about. */}
                    <span class="cbf-lct__mark stack" data-gap="3xs" data-mark
                      data-sev={flagOf(item.line)?.severity ?? ''}
                      hidden={!flagOf(item.line)}>
                      <span class="cluster" data-gap="2xs">
                        <span data-mark-sev={SEVERITIES.REQUIRED}>
                          <EsaBadge value={severityMeta[SEVERITIES.REQUIRED].short} variant={severityMeta[SEVERITIES.REQUIRED].variant} size="sm" />
                        </span>
                        <span data-mark-sev={SEVERITIES.QUESTION}>
                          <EsaBadge value={severityMeta[SEVERITIES.QUESTION].short} variant={severityMeta[SEVERITIES.QUESTION].variant} size="sm" />
                        </span>
                        <span class="cbf-lct__mark-reason" data-mark-reason>
                          {flagOf(item.line) ? reasonLabel(flagOf(item.line)!.reason) : ''}
                        </span>
                        <span data-mark-done hidden={!flagOf(item.line) || !isAddressed(review, item.line.id)}>
                          <EsaBadge value="Addressed" variant="success" size="sm" />
                        </span>
                      </span>
                      <span class="cbf-lct__mark-note" data-mark-note>{flagOf(item.line)?.note ?? ''}</span>
                      <span class="cbf-lct__note" data-mark-by>
                        {flagOf(item.line) ? `${flagOf(item.line)!.author} · ${flagOf(item.line)!.date}` : ''}
                      </span>
                      <span data-mark-address-wrap data-vendor-only hidden={!flagOf(item.line) || !vendorCanEdit(review)}>
                        <esa-checkbox size="sm" data-mark-address label="Addressed"
                          checked={isAddressed(review, item.line.id) || undefined}></esa-checkbox>
                      </span>
                    </span>
                  </div>
                </td>

                {/* ── 2. Quantity — spanned away for a lump, void for fringe ── */}
                {item.line.shape === SHAPES.LUMP ? (
                  <td class="cbf-lct__cell cbf-lct__cell--void" colspan={ENTRY_COLUMNS - 1}>
                    <div class="stack" data-gap="2xs">
                      <span class="cbf-lct__note" data-lump-note>
                        {item.line.category === 'subcontracts' ? 'Itemized on its own LIB. Its total lands here.' : 'One amount, described.'}
                      </span>
                      {/* The seam: one line HERE, the subcontract's budget THERE. */}
                      <span class="cluster" data-gap="2xs" data-sub-sheet hidden={item.line.category !== 'subcontracts'}>
                        <EsaButton size="sm" variant="secondary" appearance="soft" icon="external-link"
                          data-open-sheet={item.line.sheet ?? ''}>Open subcontract LIB</EsaButton>
                        <span class="cbf-lct__note" data-sub-status>
                          {item.line.category === 'subcontracts' ? V.subStatusText(item.line, openRequired) : ''}
                        </span>
                      </span>
                    </div>
                  </td>
                ) : item.line.shape === SHAPES.PCT_OF_BASE ? (
                  <td class="cbf-lct__cell cbf-lct__cell--void">
                    <span class="cbf-lct__void-mark">No quantity</span>
                  </td>
                ) : (
                  <td class="cbf-lct__cell cbf-lct__cell--qty">
                    <div class="stack" data-gap="2xs">
                      {/* ONE line, because it is ONE multiplication. */}
                      <span class="cluster cbf-lct__qty-chain" data-gap="2xs">
                        <span class="cluster" data-gap="2xs" data-qty-typed hidden={V.qtyLinked(item.line, lines)}>
                          <esa-text-field class="cbf-lct__field cbf-lct__field--qty" size="sm" data-field="qty"
                            value={V.numText(item.line.qty)}
                            aria-label={`Quantity — ${displayLabel(item.line)}`}></esa-text-field>
                          <esa-text-field class="cbf-lct__field cbf-lct__field--unit" size="sm" data-field="qtyUnit" data-unit-open
                            value={item.line.qtyUnit ?? ''} placeholder="Unit"
                            hidden={V.unitLocked(item.line)}
                            aria-label={`Unit — ${displayLabel(item.line)}`}></esa-text-field>
                          {/* A salary unit has to be TIME, so it is a list. */}
                          <span data-unit-select hidden={!V.unitPicked(item.line)}>
                            <esa-select class="cbf-lct__select cbf-lct__select--unit" size="sm" data-time-unit-select
                              placeholder={timeUnit(item.line).plural}
                              aria-label={`Time unit — ${displayLabel(item.line)}`}></esa-select>
                          </span>
                          <span class="cbf-lct__unit" data-unit-locked hidden={!V.unitStatic(item.line)}>{V.lockedUnit(item.line)}</span>
                        </span>

                        {/* How many people, at this time and rate — salary only. */}
                        <span class="cluster" data-gap="2xs" data-staff hidden={!isSalaryLine(item.line)}>
                          <span class="cbf-lct__times" aria-hidden="true">×</span>
                          <esa-text-field class="cbf-lct__field cbf-lct__field--staff" size="sm" data-field="staff"
                            value={V.staffText(item.line)}
                            aria-label={`Staff on this line — ${displayLabel(item.line)}`}></esa-text-field>
                          <span class="cbf-lct__unit">staff</span>
                        </span>

                        {/* The second quantity — only where the unit has one. */}
                        <span class="cluster" data-gap="2xs" data-qty2 hidden={!V.hasQty2(item.line)}>
                          <span class="cbf-lct__times" aria-hidden="true">×</span>
                          <esa-text-field class="cbf-lct__field cbf-lct__field--qty" size="sm" data-field="qty2"
                            value={V.numText(item.line.qty2)}
                            aria-label={`Second quantity — ${displayLabel(item.line)}`}></esa-text-field>
                          <esa-text-field class="cbf-lct__field cbf-lct__field--unit" size="sm" data-field="qty2Unit" data-unit2-open
                            value={item.line.qty2Unit ?? ''} placeholder="Unit"
                            hidden={V.unit2Locked(item.line)}
                            aria-label={`Second unit — ${displayLabel(item.line)}`}></esa-text-field>
                          <span class="cbf-lct__unit" data-unit2-locked hidden={!V.unit2Locked(item.line)}>{V.lockedUnit2(item.line)}</span>
                        </span>
                      </span>

                      {/* The contract period is a ceiling on time per person —
                          said only when the line is PAST it. */}
                      <span data-months-wrap hidden={!V.monthsTested(item.line) || !V.monthsOver(item.line, lines)}>
                        <EsaBadge value="Past contract period" variant="danger" size="sm" />
                      </span>

                      {/* A linked quantity is read-only and names the position. */}
                      <span class="stack" data-gap="3xs" data-qty-derived hidden={!V.qtyLinked(item.line, lines)}>
                        <span class="cbf-lct__derived" data-cell="derived-qty">
                          {`${qtyFmt(effectiveQty(item.line, lines))} ${V.lockedUnit(item.line) || item.line.qtyUnit || ''}`.trim()}
                        </span>
                        <span class="cbf-lct__note" data-cell="derived-src">{V.qtySourceText(item.line, lines)}</span>
                      </span>

                      <span class="cbf-lct__fact" data-fact="qty" hidden={V.qtyLinked(item.line, lines)}>
                        {V.qtyFactText(item.line, lines)}
                      </span>
                    </div>
                  </td>
                )}

                {/* ── 3. Rate — typed ── */}
                {item.line.shape === SHAPES.QTY_RATE && (
                  <td class="cbf-lct__cell cbf-lct__cell--rate" colspan={rateSpan(item.line)}>
                    <div class="stack" data-gap="2xs">
                      <esa-text-field
                        class:list={['cbf-lct__field', 'cbf-lct__field--rate', V.rateSuffixOf(item.line) && 'cbf-lct__field--rate-unit']}
                        size="sm" prefix="$" suffix={V.rateSuffixOf(item.line)} data-field="rate"
                        value={V.numText(item.line.rate)}
                        aria-label={`${V.rateLabelOf(item.line)} — ${displayLabel(item.line)}`}></esa-text-field>
                      <span class="cbf-lct__fact" data-fact="rate">{V.money(Number(item.line.rate) || 0)}</span>
                      {/* Where a prefilled vehicle rate came from. Stated, never
                          compared — the above-GSA flag is v2. */}
                      <span class="cbf-lct__note" data-vehicle-note hidden={!V.vehicleRateNote(item.line)}>{V.vehicleRateNote(item.line)}</span>
                    </div>
                  </td>
                )}

                {/* ── 3b. Fringe — a column, because fringe rates are read DOWN ──
                     Following the budget default it is a value; overriding is a
                     row action, which turns it into a field. */}
                {hasFringeCell(item.line) && (
                  <td class="cbf-lct__cell cbf-lct__cell--fringe">
                    <div class="stack" data-gap="2xs">
                      <div class="cluster" data-gap="2xs" data-fringe>
                        <span class="cbf-lct__derived" data-fringe-default hidden={V.fringeOverridden(item.line)}>
                          {`${V.fringePctText(item.line)}% default ·`}
                        </span>
                        <span data-fringe-input hidden={!V.fringeOverridden(item.line)}>
                          <esa-text-field class="cbf-lct__field cbf-lct__field--pct" size="sm" suffix="%" data-field="fringePct"
                            value={V.fringePctText(item.line)}
                            aria-label={`Fringe rate — ${displayLabel(item.line)}`}></esa-text-field>
                        </span>
                        <span class="cbf-lct__fact" data-fact="fringe">{V.fringeFactText(item.line)}</span>
                        <span class="cbf-lct__derived cbf-lct__fringe-amt" data-fringe-note>{V.fringeAmtText(item.line, lines, A)}</span>
                      </div>
                      <span class="cbf-lct__note" data-fringe-override hidden={!V.fringeOverridden(item.line)}>Own rate</span>
                    </div>
                  </td>
                )}

                {/* ── A fringe row's rate cell: where the number CAME FROM ── */}
                {item.line.shape === SHAPES.PCT_OF_BASE && (
                  <td class="cbf-lct__cell cbf-lct__cell--rate" colspan={rateSpan(item.line)}>
                    <div class="stack" data-gap="2xs">
                      <span class="cbf-lct__ref" data-cell="fringe-pct">{V.fringeRateText(item.line)}</span>
                      <span class="cbf-lct__note" data-cell="fringe-src">{V.fringeSrcText(item.line, lines)}</span>
                      <span class="cbf-lct__derived" data-cell="base">
                        {`${V.money(baseAmountFor(item.line, lines, A))} base · ${baseLabelFor(item.line, lines)}`}
                      </span>
                    </div>
                  </td>
                )}

                {/* ── 4. Amount — typed only for a plain lump ── */}
                <td class="cbf-lct__cell cbf-lct__cell--num">
                  {item.line.shape === SHAPES.LUMP ? (
                    <>
                      <span data-amount-edit hidden={item.line.category === 'subcontracts'}>
                        <esa-text-field class="cbf-lct__field cbf-lct__field--amount" size="sm" prefix="$" data-field="amount"
                          value={V.numText(item.line.amount)}
                          aria-label={`Amount — ${displayLabel(item.line)}`}></esa-text-field>
                      </span>
                      <strong class="cbf-lct__fact cbf-lct__money" data-fact="amount" hidden={item.line.category === 'subcontracts'}>{usd(amt(item.line.id))}</strong>
                      <strong class="cbf-lct__money" data-cell="amount" hidden={item.line.category !== 'subcontracts'}>{usd(amt(item.line.id))}</strong>
                    </>
                  ) : (
                    <strong class="cbf-lct__money" data-cell="amount">{usd(amt(item.line.id))}</strong>
                  )}
                </td>

                {/* ── 5. Row action — the vendor's menu, the COR's mark ──
                     The same slot, because they are the one operation each role
                     performs on a line. */}
                <td class="cbf-lct__cell cbf-lct__cell--act">
                  <span class="cbf-lct__hover" data-row-menu-wrap data-vendor-only hidden={V.derivedRow(item.line)}>
                    <esa-dropdown-menu position="below-end" data-row-menu>
                      <EsaButton variant="chrome" size="sm" class="cbf-lct__kebab"
                        aria-label={`Actions for this line — ${displayLabel(item.line) || 'new line'}`}
                        title={`Actions for this line — ${displayLabel(item.line) || 'new line'}`}>
                        <EsaIcon name="ellipsis-vertical" paths={KEBAB_PATHS} size="sm" />
                      </EsaButton>
                    </esa-dropdown-menu>
                  </span>

                  <span data-mark-cell hidden>
                    <esa-popover position="left" trigger="click" offset="6" data-mark-popover>
                      <span data-mark-state="off" hidden={!!flagOf(item.line)}>
                        <EsaButton variant="chrome" iconOnly icon="pencil" size="sm"
                          label={`Mark this line for the vendor — ${displayLabel(item.line) || 'new line'}`} />
                      </span>
                      <span data-mark-state="on" hidden={!flagOf(item.line)}>
                        <EsaButton variant="chrome" iconOnly icon="triangle-alert" size="sm"
                          label={`Edit the mark on this line — ${displayLabel(item.line) || 'new line'}`} />
                      </span>
                      <div slot="content" class="cbf-lct__markform stack" data-gap="sm" data-mark-panel>
                        <span class="cbf-lct__panel-head">Mark this line for the vendor</span>
                        <span class="cbf-lct__note" data-mark-form-line>{displayLabel(item.line)}</span>
                        <esa-radio-group data-mark-sev-input size="md" label="Type of mark"></esa-radio-group>
                        <esa-select data-mark-reason-input size="md" label="Reason" placeholder="Pick a reason"></esa-select>
                        <esa-textarea data-mark-note-input label="Note to the vendor" rows="3" auto-resize
                          help-text="Say what to change, not just what’s wrong."
                          value={flagOf(item.line)?.note ?? ''}></esa-textarea>
                        <span class="repel" data-gap="sm">
                          <span data-mark-remove hidden={!flagOf(item.line)}>
                            <EsaButton size="sm" variant="ghost">Remove mark</EsaButton>
                          </span>
                          <span data-mark-save>
                            <EsaButton size="sm" variant="primary">Save mark</EsaButton>
                          </span>
                        </span>
                      </div>
                    </esa-popover>
                  </span>
                </td>
              </tr>
            ),
          )}
        </tbody>
      ))}

      {/* ── The close: direct, indirect base, indirect, and the total ── */}
      <tfoot class="cbf-lct__totals">
        {/* The vendor cannot see Personnel — fringe, so the foot reports its
            subtotal; the section heads they CAN see then add up. */}
        <tr data-fringe-rollup>
          <th scope="row" colspan={ENTRY_COLUMNS}>
            Personnel — fringe
            <span class="cbf-lct__note">Generated from the salary lines above, at the fringe rate on each.</span>
          </th>
          <td class="cbf-lct__cell cbf-lct__cell--num">
            <span data-cat-total="personnel-fringe">{usd(priced.byCategory['personnel-fringe'] ?? 0)}</span>
          </td>
          <td class="cbf-lct__cell"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row" colspan={ENTRY_COLUMNS}>
            Direct cost
            <span class="cbf-lct__note">Sum of every cost line above.</span>
          </th>
          <td class="cbf-lct__cell cbf-lct__cell--num"><span data-total="direct">{usd(t0.direct)}</span></td>
          <td class="cbf-lct__cell"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr data-indirect-row hidden={isSub}>
          <th scope="row" colspan={ENTRY_COLUMNS}>
            Indirect base
            <span class="cbf-lct__note" data-indirect-scope>{V.scopeText(cfg)}</span>
          </th>
          <td class="cbf-lct__cell cbf-lct__cell--num"><span data-total="indirectBase">{usd(t0.indirectBase)}</span></td>
          <td class="cbf-lct__cell"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr data-indirect-row hidden={isSub}>
          <th scope="row" colspan={ENTRY_COLUMNS}>
            Indirect at <span data-indirect-rate>{pct(cfg.rate)}</span>
            <span class="cbf-lct__note" data-indirect-ref>{V.indirectRefText(cfg)}</span>
          </th>
          <td class="cbf-lct__cell cbf-lct__cell--num"><span data-total="indirect">{usd(t0.indirect)}</span></td>
          <td class="cbf-lct__cell"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="cbf-lct__grand">
          <th scope="row" colspan={ENTRY_COLUMNS}>
            {isSub ? 'Subcontract total' : 'Total this contract period'}
            <span class="cbf-lct__note" data-total-note hidden={isSub}>
              {`${pct(t0.pctOfValue, 1)} of the ${usd(contract.contractValue)} Contract Value · ${usd(t0.remaining)} remaining`}
            </span>
          </th>
          {/* A span, not <strong>: the Astro compiler treats a <strong> in the
              table's last cell as still open and re-opens it after </table>. */}
          <td class="cbf-lct__cell cbf-lct__cell--num"><span class="cbf-lct__grand-total" data-total="total">{usd(t0.total)}</span></td>
          <td class="cbf-lct__cell"></td>
        </tr>
      </tfoot>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

{/* Without the script nothing can unfold a section, so the server-rendered
    budget shows whole. */}
<noscript><style is:inline>tbody[data-collapsed] > tr { display: table-row !important; }</style></noscript>

{/* ── The budget's default fringe rate ──
    One small dialog, because the change reaches every position that follows
    the default — it says so before it is saved. */}
<esa-dialog data-fringe-dialog size="sm" heading="Default fringe rate">
  <div class="stack" data-gap="sm">
    <esa-text-field data-fringe-default-field size="md" label="Default rate" suffix="%"></esa-text-field>
  </div>
  <div slot="footer" class="cluster cbf-lct__dialog-actions" data-gap="sm">
    <span data-fringe-cancel><EsaButton size="sm" variant="secondary" appearance="outline">Cancel</EsaButton></span>
    <span data-fringe-save><EsaButton size="sm" variant="primary">Save</EsaButton></span>
  </div>
</esa-dialog>

<script>
  import * as V from '../../lib/lib-mvp-view';
  import '@esa/ecology/esa-text-field';
  import '@esa/ecology/esa-select';
  import '@esa/ecology/esa-popover';
  import '@esa/ecology/esa-dropdown-menu';
  import '@esa/ecology/esa-dialog';
  import '@esa/ecology/esa-radio-group';
  import '@esa/ecology/esa-textarea';
  import '@esa/ecology/esa-checkbox';
  import { withBase } from '../../lib/base';
  import {
    SEVERITIES,
    REASONS,
    severityMeta,
    reasonLabel,
    loadReview,
    saveReview,
    fireReview,
    flagFor,
    isAddressed,
    setFlag,
    removeFlag,
    setAddressed,
    vendorCanEdit,
    corCanMark,
    isLocked,
    openRequiredFlags,
  } from '../../data/lib-mvp-review.mjs';
  import {
    EVENTS,
    SHAPES,
    contract,
    categories,
    costLines,
    indirectConfig,
    budgetRules,
    activateBudget,
    subcontractSheets,
    syncSubcontractAmounts,
    subIndirectCfg,
    withResolvedIndirect,
    priceLines,
    effectiveQty,
    baseAmountFor,
    baseLabelFor,
    dependentsOf,
    categoryFixedUnit,
    timeUnit,
    isSalaryLine,
    titleOfLine,
    travelKind,
    vehicleKind,
    meetingKind,
    otherKind,
    VEHICLE_KINDS,
    MEETING_KINDS,
    OTHER_KINDS,
    prefillVehicleRate,
    linkQtyTo,
    detachQty,
    refollowQty,
    syncFringeLines,
    fringeDefaults,
    isFringeOverride,
    hasFringeCell,
    rateSpan,
    blockOf,
    submitChecksFor,
    advisoriesFor,
    usd,
    pct,
    qtyFmt,
  } from '../../data/lib-mvp.mjs';
  import { isBlank, blankConfig } from '../../data/lib-mvp-demo.mjs';

  const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-lct]');
  if (root) init(root);

  function init(root: HTMLElement) {
    const $ = <T extends HTMLElement = HTMLElement>(sel: string, scope: ParentNode = root) =>
      scope.querySelector<T>(sel);
    const $$ = (sel: string, scope: ParentNode = root) => Array.from(scope.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(sel));

    /* ── Row templates, captured and taken out before anything reads rows ── */
    const rowTemplates: Record<string, HTMLTableRowElement> = {};
    const tplBody = $('tbody[data-tpl]');
    $$('tr[data-shape]', tplBody ?? root).forEach((tr) => {
      if (tplBody) rowTemplates[tr.dataset.shape!] = tr.cloneNode(true) as HTMLTableRowElement;
    });
    const fringeCellTemplate = (tplBody?.querySelector('.cbf-lct__cell--fringe') as HTMLTableCellElement | null)
      ?.cloneNode(true) as HTMLTableCellElement | undefined;
    tplBody?.remove();

    /* ── Which budget, and its working copy ─────────────────────────────────
       A subcontract page swaps the data module to that child LIB (its lines,
       its sections, no indirect) before anything reads it. Edits then mutate
       THIS copy, never the module's exports. */
    const budgetId = root.dataset.budget ?? 'main';
    activateBudget(budgetId);
    const isSub = budgetRules.kind === 'subcontract';

    /* The parent reads every stored child LIB, so the totals they carry reach
       its subcontract lines — priceLines prices a subcontract line from its
       sheet. Stored lines carry their generated fringe lines, priced at the
       child's own rates; they are not re-synced against this page's default. */
    if (!isSub) {
      V.storedBudgetIds().forEach((id) => {
        const sheet = (subcontractSheets as any)[id];
        const stored = id !== 'main' && sheet ? V.loadStoredLines(id) : null;
        if (stored) sheet.lines = stored.lines;
      });
    }

    const stored = V.loadStoredLines(budgetId);
    const blank = !isSub && isBlank();
    if (stored?.fringePct != null) fringeDefaults.pct = stored.fringePct;
    const lines: any[] = stored
      ? structuredClone(stored.lines)
      : blank ? [] : structuredClone(costLines);
    let cfg: any = isSub ? subIndirectCfg() : blank ? blankConfig() : { ...indirectConfig, appliesTo: [...indirectConfig.appliesTo] };

    /* A subcontract's name belongs to its details (another surface, which
       stores it); the parent line follows it. */
    if (!isSub) {
      lines.filter((l) => l.category === 'subcontracts' && l.sheet).forEach((l) => {
        try {
          const raw = sessionStorage.getItem(`cbf-libmvp-sheet:${l.sheet}`);
          const name = raw ? String(JSON.parse(raw)?.name ?? '').trim() : '';
          if (name) l.label = name;
        } catch { /* no stored details */ }
      });
    }

    let seq = 0;
    const newId = () => `${budgetId === 'main' ? 'new' : `${budgetId}-new`}-${++seq}-${Date.now().toString(36)}`;
    const rowOf = (id: string) => $(`tr[data-line="${CSS.escape(id)}"]`);
    const lineById = (id: string) => lines.find((l) => l.id === id);
    const num = (s: string) => {
      const v = parseFloat(String(s ?? '').replace(/[^0-9.\-]/g, ''));
      return Number.isFinite(v) ? v : 0;
    };

    /* ── View derivations — the SAME bodies the frontmatter uses ── */
    const displayLabel = (l: any) => V.displayLabel(l, lines);
    /* Keep the stored label in step with a derived one, so the review panel —
       which addresses lines BY NAME — never quotes a name the grid stopped
       showing. Mutates, so it is local rather than a view derivation. */
    const syncLabel = (l: any) => {
      if (l.category === 'travel' || l.category === 'vehicles' || l.category === 'personnel-fringe') l.label = displayLabel(l);
    };

    /* ── Tiny DOM setters (esa-* internals are stable markup) ── */
    const show = (el: Element | null, on: boolean) => { if (el) (el as HTMLElement).hidden = !on; };
    const setText = (el: Element | null, text: string) => { if (el && el.textContent !== text) el.textContent = text; };
    /** esa-field-error renders <p.esa-field-error><span.esa-field-error__text>. */
    const setErrText = (wrap: Element | null, text: string) => setText(wrap?.querySelector('.esa-field-error__text') ?? null, text);
    /** esa-badge renders <span.esa-badge><span.esa-badge__text>. */
    const setBadgeText = (wrap: Element | null, text: string) => setText(wrap?.querySelector('.esa-badge__text') ?? null, text);

    /* ── Who is reading, and what they may do ────────────────────────────────
       The vendor edits in draft / returned; the COR marks while in review.
       Everyone else reads the facts lens. */
    let review: any = loadReview();
    const role = () => (document.documentElement.dataset.cbfRole === 'cor' ? 'cor' : 'vendor');
    const canEdit = () => role() === 'vendor' && vendorCanEdit(review);
    const canMark = () => role() === 'cor' && corCanMark(review);
    const markOf = (id: string) => {
      const f = flagFor(review, id);
      return f && (f.budget ?? 'main') === budgetId ? f : null;
    };
    const openRequired = () => openRequiredFlags(review);

    const paintPermissions = () => {
      const cor = role() === 'cor';
      if (canEdit()) root.removeAttribute('data-lens'); else root.dataset.lens = 'read';
      show($('[data-notice="in-review"]'), !cor && review.status === 'in-review');
      show($('[data-notice="approved"]'), isLocked(review));
      show($('[data-notice="cor-wait"]'), cor && !corCanMark(review) && !isLocked(review));
      $$('[data-mark-cell]').forEach((el) => show(el, canMark()));
    };

    /* ── The COR's mark editor ── */
    const SEV_OPTIONS = [
      { label: severityMeta[SEVERITIES.REQUIRED].label, value: SEVERITIES.REQUIRED },
      { label: severityMeta[SEVERITIES.QUESTION].label, value: SEVERITIES.QUESTION },
    ];
    const REASON_OPTIONS = REASONS.map((r: any) => ({ label: r.label, value: r.key }));

    const fillMarkForm = (tr: HTMLElement, line: any) => {
      const f = markOf(line.id);
      const sev: any = $('[data-mark-sev-input]', tr);
      if (sev) { sev.options = SEV_OPTIONS; sev.value = f?.severity ?? SEVERITIES.REQUIRED; }
      const reason: any = $('[data-mark-reason-input]', tr);
      if (reason) { reason.options = REASON_OPTIONS; reason.value = f?.reason ?? ''; }
      const note: any = $('[data-mark-note-input]', tr);
      if (note) note.value = f?.note ?? '';
      setText($('[data-mark-form-line]', tr), displayLabel(line) || 'Untitled line');
    };

    const paintMark = (tr: HTMLElement | null, line: any) => {
      if (!tr) return;
      const f = markOf(line.id);
      const band = $('[data-mark]', tr);
      show(band, !!f);
      if (band) band.dataset.sev = f?.severity ?? '';
      const done = !!f && isAddressed(review, line.id);
      if (f) {
        setText($('[data-mark-reason]', tr), reasonLabel(f.reason));
        setText($('[data-mark-note]', tr), f.note || 'No note written.');
        setText($('[data-mark-by]', tr), `${f.author} · ${f.date}`);
      }
      show($('[data-mark-done]', tr), done);
      show($('[data-mark-address-wrap]', tr), !!f && role() === 'vendor' && vendorCanEdit(review));
      const box: any = $('[data-mark-address]', tr);
      if (box) box.checked = done;
      show($('[data-mark-state="off"]', tr), !f);
      show($('[data-mark-state="on"]', tr), !!f);
      show($('[data-mark-remove]', tr), !!f);
    };
    const paintReview = () => lines.forEach((l) => paintMark(rowOf(l.id), l));

    /** The grid changed a mark: write it, tell everyone, repaint. */
    const commitReview = (next: any) => {
      review = next;
      saveReview(review);
      paintReview();
      fireReview(review);
      recompute();
    };

    /* ── Painting: fillRow writes identity + entry VALUES (never while typing),
       paintRow writes everything DERIVED. ── */
    const fillRow = (tr: HTMLElement, line: any) => {
      tr.dataset.line = line.id;
      tr.dataset.shape = line.shape;
      tr.dataset.cat = line.category;
      tr.dataset.block = blockOf(line);

      /* Reconcile the cell COUNT first: the qty-rate template is shared by the
         one category with a fringe cell and the ones that span over it. */
      const rateCell = $('.cbf-lct__cell--rate', tr) as HTMLTableCellElement | null;
      let fringeCell = $('.cbf-lct__cell--fringe', tr) as HTMLTableCellElement | null;
      if (hasFringeCell(line) && !fringeCell && fringeCellTemplate) {
        fringeCell = fringeCellTemplate.cloneNode(true) as HTMLTableCellElement;
        rateCell?.after(fringeCell);
      } else if (!hasFringeCell(line) && fringeCell) {
        fringeCell.remove();
      }
      if (rateCell) rateCell.colSpan = rateSpan(line);

      const isSubLine = line.category === 'subcontracts';
      show($('[data-sub-sheet]', tr), isSubLine);
      const open = $('[data-open-sheet]', tr);
      if (open) open.dataset.openSheet = line.sheet ?? '';
      setText($('[data-lump-note]', tr), isSubLine ? 'Itemized on its own LIB. Its total lands here.' : 'One amount, described.');
      show($('[data-amount-edit]', tr), line.shape === SHAPES.LUMP && !isSubLine);

      $$('[data-field]', tr).forEach((el: any) => {
        const key = el.dataset.field;
        if (key === 'label' || key === 'destination' || key === 'desc' || key === 'qtyUnit' || key === 'qty2Unit') el.value = line[key] ?? '';
        else if (key === 'fringePct') el.value = V.fringePctText(line);
        else if (key === 'staff') el.value = V.staffText(line);
        else el.value = V.numText(line[key]);
      });
      const label: any = $('[data-field="label"]', tr);
      if (label) label.placeholder = V.labelPlaceholderOf(line);
      const desc: any = $('[data-field="desc"]', tr);
      if (desc) desc.placeholder = V.descPlaceholderOf(line);

      /* Option lists are constant, so they are safe to seed on every fill. */
      const seed = (sel: string, options: any[], value: string) => {
        const el: any = $(sel, tr);
        if (el) { el.options = options; el.value = value ?? ''; }
      };
      seed('[data-time-unit-select]', V.timeUnitOptions(), timeUnit(line).key);
      seed('[data-travel-kind-select]', V.travelKindOptions(), line.travelKind);
      seed('[data-vehicle-kind-select]', V.vehicleKindOptions(), line.vehicleKind);
      seed('[data-vehicle-type-select]', V.vehicleTypeOptions(), line.vehicleType);
      seed('[data-meeting-kind-select]', V.meetingKindOptions(), line.meetingKind);
      seed('[data-other-kind-select]', V.otherKindOptions(), line.otherKind);
    };

    /* ── A row's menu, built for THIS line in its CURRENT state ──────────────
       Only what the line can do: override or reset its fringe, follow / stop
       following / re-follow a position's time, move between supplies and
       capital equipment. Delete is last and set apart. */
    const rowMenuItems = (line: any) => {
      const items: any[] = [];
      const add = (label: string, act: string) => items.push({ label, action: `row|${act}` });
      if (isSalaryLine(line)) {
        if (V.fringeOverridden(line)) add(V.fringeResetText(), 'fringe-reset');
        else add('Override fringe rate', 'fringe-override');
      }
      if (V.qtyLinked(line, lines)) {
        add('Use my own quantity', 'detach-qty');
      } else {
        const was = V.detachedSource(line, lines);
        if (was) add(`Follow ${titleOfLine(was) || 'the untitled position'} again`, 'refollow-qty');
        V.linkOptions(line, lines).forEach((s: any) =>
          add(`Quantity follows ${titleOfLine(s) || 'an untitled position'}`, `link|${s.id}`));
      }
      if (line.category === 'supplies') add(V.moveClassText(line), 'move-class');
      if (items.length) items.push({ divider: true });
      items.push({ label: 'Delete line', action: 'row|delete', variant: 'danger' });
      return items;
    };

    /* Every control on a row names its line ("Quantity — PIT tags"). A new row
       is a CLONE, so the part after " — " is rewritten from the line as it is. */
    const relabelRow = (tr: HTMLElement, line: any) => {
      const name = displayLabel(line) || 'new line';
      tr.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[aria-label], [title]').forEach((el) => {
        ['aria-label', 'title'].forEach((attr) => {
          const cur = el.getAttribute(attr);
          if (!cur || !cur.includes(' — ')) return;
          const next = `${cur.split(' — ')[0]} — ${name}`;
          if (next !== cur) el.setAttribute(attr, next);
        });
      });
    };

    const paintRow = (tr: HTMLElement | null, line: any, priced: any) => {
      if (!tr) return;
      relabelRow(tr, line);
      const a = priced.amounts;
      const cat = line.category;

      /* Identity — reveal the controls that name a line in THIS category. */
      show($('[data-kind-pick="travel"]', tr), cat === 'travel');
      show($('[data-kind-pick="vehicles"]', tr), cat === 'vehicles');
      show($('[data-kind-pick="meetings"]', tr), cat === 'meetings');
      show($('[data-kind-pick="other"]', tr), cat === 'other' && line.shape === SHAPES.QTY_RATE);
      show($('[data-vehicle-type]', tr), V.takesVehicleType(line));
      show($('[data-ident-label]', tr), V.identOf(line) === 'label');
      show($('[data-travel-dest]', tr), cat === 'travel');
      show($('[data-desc]', tr), V.takesDesc(line));
      const derived = $('[data-cell="ident-derived"]', tr);
      show(derived, V.identOf(line) === 'derived');
      setText(derived, displayLabel(line));
      setText($('[data-fact="label"]', tr), displayLabel(line) || 'Untitled line');
      const descFact = $('[data-fact="desc"]', tr);
      show(descFact, V.isPlainLump(line) && !!(line.desc ?? '').trim());
      setText(descFact, line.desc ?? '');
      show($('[data-vendor-badge]', tr), V.vendorDefined(line));

      /* Inline validation, the first thing the line still needs. */
      const err = V.lineErrors(line, lines)[0] ?? '';
      const errWrap = $('[data-line-err]', tr);
      show(errWrap, !!err);
      if (err) setErrText(errWrap, err);

      /* Quantity — typed, or linked and named. */
      const linked = V.qtyLinked(line, lines);
      show($('[data-qty-typed]', tr), !linked);
      show($('[data-qty-derived]', tr), linked);
      setText($('[data-cell="derived-qty"]', tr), `${qtyFmt(effectiveQty(line, lines))} ${V.lockedUnit(line) || line.qtyUnit || ''}`.trim());
      setText($('[data-cell="derived-src"]', tr), V.qtySourceText(line, lines));
      show($('[data-unit-open]', tr), !V.unitLocked(line));
      show($('[data-unit-select]', tr), V.unitPicked(line));
      const locked = $('[data-unit-locked]', tr);
      show(locked, V.unitStatic(line));
      setText(locked, V.lockedUnit(line));
      show($('[data-staff]', tr), isSalaryLine(line));
      show($('[data-qty2]', tr), V.hasQty2(line));
      show($('[data-unit2-open]', tr), !V.unit2Locked(line));
      const locked2 = $('[data-unit2-locked]', tr);
      show(locked2, V.unit2Locked(line));
      setText(locked2, V.lockedUnit2(line));
      show($('[data-months-wrap]', tr), V.monthsTested(line) && V.monthsOver(line, lines));
      const qtyFact = $('[data-fact="qty"]', tr);
      show(qtyFact, !linked);
      setText(qtyFact, V.qtyFactText(line, lines));

      /* Rate — its unit rides the box; a vehicle says where its default came from. */
      const rateField: any = $('[data-field="rate"]', tr);
      if (rateField) {
        const suffix = V.rateSuffixOf(line);
        rateField.suffix = suffix;
        rateField.classList.toggle('cbf-lct__field--rate-unit', !!suffix);
      }
      setText($('[data-fact="rate"]', tr), V.money(Number(line.rate) || 0));
      const vNote = $('[data-vehicle-note]', tr);
      show(vNote, !!V.vehicleRateNote(line));
      setText(vNote, V.vehicleRateNote(line));

      /* Fringe, on the row that decides it, with the dollars it generates. */
      if ($('[data-fringe]', tr)) {
        const ovr = V.fringeOverridden(line);
        show($('[data-fringe-input]', tr), ovr);
        show($('[data-fringe-override]', tr), ovr);
        const dflt = $('[data-fringe-default]', tr);
        show(dflt, !ovr);
        setText(dflt, `${V.fringePctText(line)}% default ·`);
        setText($('[data-fact="fringe"]', tr), V.fringeFactText(line));
        setText($('[data-fringe-note]', tr), V.fringeAmtText(line, lines, a));
      }
      if ($('[data-cell="base"]', tr)) {
        setText($('[data-cell="fringe-pct"]', tr), V.fringeRateText(line));
        setText($('[data-cell="fringe-src"]', tr), V.fringeSrcText(line, lines));
        setText($('[data-cell="base"]', tr), `${V.money(baseAmountFor(line, lines, a))} base · ${baseLabelFor(line, lines)}`);
      }

      /* Amount, and — on a subcontract — how its child LIB stands. */
      setText($('[data-cell="amount"]', tr), usd(a[line.id] ?? 0));
      setText($('[data-fact="amount"]', tr), usd(a[line.id] ?? 0));
      if (cat === 'subcontracts') setText($('[data-sub-status]', tr), V.subStatusText(line, openRequired()));

      /* Inline tint — never a colored left border — for blocking states only. */
      const flag = V.rowFlag(line, lines);
      if (flag) tr.dataset.flag = flag; else tr.removeAttribute('data-flag');

      show($('[data-row-menu-wrap]', tr), !V.derivedRow(line));
      const menu: any = $('[data-row-menu]', tr);
      if (menu && !V.derivedRow(line)) menu.items = rowMenuItems(line);
    };

    const paintGroups = (priced: any) => {
      categories.forEach((cat: any) => {
        /* All of them: fringe reports its subtotal on its own head and in the foot. */
        $$(`[data-cat-total="${cat.key}"]`).forEach((el) => setText(el, usd(priced.byCategory[cat.key] ?? 0)));
        (cat.blocks ?? []).forEach((b: any) => {
          const k = `${cat.key}:${b.key}`;
          setText($(`[data-block-total="${k}"]`), usd(priced.byBlock[k] ?? 0));
        });
        /* What a folded section still owes the reader: how many lines, and
           whether any of them needs a fix. */
        const tb = $(`tbody[data-cat="${cat.key}"]`);
        if (!tb) return;
        const inCat = lines.filter((l) => l.category === cat.key);
        setText($('[data-cat-count]', tb), inCat.length ? `${inCat.length} line${inCat.length === 1 ? '' : 's'}` : 'No lines');
        const bad = inCat.filter((l) => V.lineErrors(l, lines).length || V.subIssuesOf(l, openRequired()).length).length;
        const badge = $('[data-cat-issues]', tb);
        show(badge, bad > 0);
        if (bad) setBadgeText(badge, `${bad} need${bad === 1 ? 's' : ''} attention`);
      });
      const fb = $('[data-fringe-badge]');
      const fbText = V.fringeBadge();
      show(fb, !!fbText);
      if (fbText) setBadgeText(fb, fbText);
    };

    const paintTotals = (t: any) => {
      setText($('[data-total="direct"]'), usd(t.direct));
      setText($('[data-total="indirectBase"]'), usd(t.indirectBase));
      setText($('[data-total="indirect"]'), usd(t.indirect));
      setText($('[data-total="total"]'), usd(t.total));
      setText($('[data-indirect-rate]'), pct(cfg.rate));
      setText($('[data-indirect-ref]'), V.indirectRefText(cfg));
      setText($('[data-indirect-scope]'), V.scopeText(cfg));
      if (!isSub) setText($('[data-total-note]'),
        `${pct(t.pctOfValue, 1)} of the ${usd(contract.contractValue)} Contract Value · ${
          t.remaining >= 0 ? `${usd(t.remaining)} remaining` : `${usd(Math.abs(t.remaining))} over`}`);
    };

    /* ── Autosave: the store, then the "Saved" signal ── */
    const persist = () => V.saveStoredLines(budgetId, { lines, fringePct: fringeDefaults.pct });
    let savedTimer = 0;
    const showSaved = () => {
      const el = $('[data-saved]');
      show(el, true);
      window.clearTimeout(savedTimer);
      savedTimer = window.setTimeout(() => show(el, false), 2500);
    };

    /** The one broadcast the reconciliation rail and the review panel consume. */
    const fireTotals = (t: any) => {
      document.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent(EVENTS.totals, {
        detail: {
          budget: budgetId,
          total: t.total,
          direct: t.direct,
          indirect: t.indirect,
          indirectBase: t.indirectBase,
          remaining: t.remaining,
          pctOfValue: t.pctOfValue,
          checks: submitChecksFor(lines, cfg, { openRequired: openRequired(), budgetId }),
          advisories: advisoriesFor(lines, cfg),
          lines,
        },
      }));
    };

    /* The money moment: the rows that just moved because of THIS edit flash. */
    const flash = (els: (HTMLElement | null)[]) => {
      els.filter(Boolean).forEach((el) => {
        const node = el as HTMLElement;
        node.classList.remove('is-recomputed');
        void node.offsetWidth;
        node.classList.add('is-recomputed');
        window.setTimeout(() => node.classList.remove('is-recomputed'), 1500);
      });
    };

    /* ── Mounting a row for a line: clone its shape, file it, fill it ── */
    const insertRow = (tr: HTMLElement, line: any) => {
      const tbody = $(`tbody[data-cat="${line.category}"]`);
      if (!tbody) return false;
      const block = blockOf(line);
      if (block) {
        const rows = $$(`tr[data-line][data-block="${block}"]`, tbody).filter((r) => r !== tr);
        const anchor = rows[rows.length - 1] ?? $(`tr[data-blockhead="${block}"]`, tbody);
        if (anchor) anchor.after(tr); else tbody.appendChild(tr);
      } else {
        tbody.appendChild(tr);
      }
      return true;
    };
    const mountRow = (line: any): HTMLTableRowElement | null => {
      const tpl = rowTemplates[line.shape];
      if (!tpl) return null;
      const tr = tpl.cloneNode(true) as HTMLTableRowElement;
      if (!insertRow(tr, line)) return null;
      fillRow(tr, line);
      fillMarkForm(tr, line);
      paintMark(tr, line);
      wireRow(tr);
      return tr;
    };

    /* ── Keep the generated Fringe section in step with the salary section ── */
    let fringeSig = '';
    const syncFringeRows = () => {
      syncFringeLines(lines);
      const want = lines.filter((l) => l.category === 'personnel-fringe');
      const sig = want.map((l) => l.id).join('|');
      if (sig === fringeSig) return;
      fringeSig = sig;
      const tbody = $('tbody[data-cat="personnel-fringe"]');
      if (!tbody) return;
      const wanted = new Set(want.map((l) => l.id));
      $$('tr[data-line]', tbody).forEach((tr) => { if (!wanted.has(tr.dataset.line!)) tr.remove(); });
      want.forEach((line) => {
        const tr = rowOf(line.id) ?? mountRow(line);
        if (tr) tbody.appendChild(tr);
      });
    };

    /* ── Folding sections — folded by default, remembered for the session ── */
    const FOLD_KEY = 'cbf-libmvp-open-sections';
    const readOpen = (): string[] => {
      try { return JSON.parse(sessionStorage.getItem(FOLD_KEY) ?? '[]'); } catch { return []; }
    };
    const writeOpen = () => {
      try {
        const open = $$('tbody[data-cat]').filter((tb) => !tb.hasAttribute('data-collapsed')).map((tb) => tb.dataset.cat!);
        sessionStorage.setItem(FOLD_KEY, JSON.stringify(open));
      } catch { /* storage unavailable — folding still works for this view */ }
    };
    const setFolded = (tbody: HTMLElement | null, folded: boolean, remember = true) => {
      if (!tbody) return;
      tbody.toggleAttribute('data-collapsed', folded);
      $('[data-cat-toggle] button', tbody)?.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(!folded));
      if (remember) writeOpen();
    };
    const unfoldTo = (el: Element | null | undefined) => {
      const tb = el?.closest('tbody[data-cat]') as HTMLElement | null;
      if (tb?.hasAttribute('data-collapsed')) setFolded(tb, false);
    };
    {
      const open = readOpen();
      $$('tbody[data-cat]').forEach((tb) => setFolded(tb, !open.includes(tb.dataset.cat!), false));
    }

    /* ── The first-run state ── */
    const paintEmpty = () => {
      const none = !lines.some((l) => !V.derivedRow(l));
      const wrap = $('[data-empty]');
      show(wrap, none);
      if (none) setText(wrap?.querySelector('.esa-empty-state__description') ?? null,
        canEdit() ? 'Add a line to any section below.' : 'Nothing has been entered on this budget.');
    };

    /**
     * Re-price everything and repaint. `commit` marks a vendor's edit: those
     * also flash the rows that moved and show "Saved". The store is written
     * every time, BEFORE totals go out — the subcontract details read the child
     * lines from it when they hear totals.
     */
    const recompute = (originId?: string, { commit = false } = {}) => {
      syncFringeRows();
      if (!isSub) syncSubcontractAmounts(lines);
      const priced = priceLines(lines, cfg);
      lines.forEach((l) => paintRow(rowOf(l.id), l, priced));
      paintGroups(priced);
      paintTotals(priced.totals);
      paintEmpty();
      persist();
      fireTotals(priced.totals);
      if (commit) showSaved();
      if (originId) flash(dependentsOf(originId, lines).map((l: any) => rowOf(l.id)));
      return priced;
    };
    const commitEdit = (originId?: string) => recompute(originId, { commit: true });

    /* ── The mark editor's own clicks ──
       esa-popover toggles on any click inside its anchor while the slotted panel
       sits INSIDE that anchor, so the panel stops propagation and its Save and
       Remove are handled here. Known hub gap, logged in docs/hub-issues.md. */
    function wireRow(tr: HTMLElement) {
      $$('[data-mark-panel]', tr).forEach((panel) =>
        panel.addEventListener('click', (ev) => {
          const t = ev.target as HTMLElement;
          if (t.closest('[data-mark-save]')) saveMark(tr);
          else if (t.closest('[data-mark-remove]')) removeMark(tr);
          ev.stopPropagation();
        }),
      );
    }
    const closeMark = (tr: HTMLElement) => {
      const pop: any = $('[data-mark-popover]', tr);
      if (pop) pop.open = false;
    };
    const saveMark = (tr: HTMLElement) => {
      const line = lineById(tr.dataset.line!);
      if (!line || !canMark()) return;
      const sev = ($('[data-mark-sev-input]', tr) as any)?.value;
      commitReview(setFlag(review, {
        lineId: line.id,
        budget: budgetId,
        severity: sev === SEVERITIES.QUESTION ? SEVERITIES.QUESTION : SEVERITIES.REQUIRED,
        reason: ($('[data-mark-reason-input]', tr) as any)?.value || 'other',
        note: String(($('[data-mark-note-input]', tr) as any)?.value ?? '').trim(),
      }));
      closeMark(tr);
    };
    const removeMark = (tr: HTMLElement) => {
      const line = lineById(tr.dataset.line!);
      if (!line || !canMark()) return;
      commitReview(removeFlag(review, line.id));
      fillMarkForm(tr, line);
      closeMark(tr);
    };

    /* ── The kinds own the units ─────────────────────────────────────────────
       Changing a kind resets what it fixes rather than leaving a lodging line's
       "nights" on an airfare line. */
    const applyTravelKind = (line: any, key: string) => {
      const k = travelKind(key);
      line.travelKind = key;
      if (!k) return;
      line.qtyUnit = k.countLabel;
      if (k.durationLabel) { line.qty2 = line.qty2 ?? 1; line.qty2Unit = k.durationLabel; }
      else { delete line.qty2; delete line.qty2Unit; }
      if (k.vendorDefined) line.desc = line.desc ?? ''; else delete line.desc;
      line.destination = line.destination ?? '';
      line.rate = line.rate ?? 0;
      syncLabel(line);
    };
    /* A vehicle kind fixes the unit(s); with a type it PREFILLS the GSA rate as
       an editable default — never over a number the vendor typed. */
    const applyVehicleKind = (line: any, key: string) => {
      const prev = { vehicleKind: line.vehicleKind, vehicleType: line.vehicleType };
      const k = vehicleKind(key);
      line.vehicleKind = key;
      if (!k) return;
      if (k.unit) line.qtyUnit = k.unit;
      else if (VEHICLE_KINDS.some((x: any) => x.unit && x.unit === line.qtyUnit)) line.qtyUnit = '';
      if (k.secondUnit) { line.qty2 = line.qty2 ?? 1; line.qty2Unit = k.secondUnit; }
      else { delete line.qty2; delete line.qty2Unit; }
      if (k.vendorDefined) { delete line.vehicleType; line.desc = line.desc ?? ''; } else delete line.desc;
      prefillVehicleRate(line, prev);
      syncLabel(line);
    };
    const applyCostKind = (line: any, key: string) => {
      const k = line.category === 'meetings' ? meetingKind(key) : otherKind(key);
      if (line.category === 'meetings') line.meetingKind = key; else line.otherKind = key;
      if (!k) return;
      if (k.unit) line.qtyUnit = k.unit;
      else if (line.qtyUnit && [...MEETING_KINDS, ...OTHER_KINDS].some((x: any) => x.unit === line.qtyUnit)) line.qtyUnit = '';
      if (k.secondUnit) { line.qty2 = line.qty2 ?? 1; line.qty2Unit = k.secondUnit; }
      else { delete line.qty2; delete line.qty2Unit; }
    };

    /* ── Add a line INLINE — no modal ── */
    const addLine = (catKey: string, block: string, shape: string, kind = '') => {
      if (!canEdit()) return;
      const line: any = { id: newId(), category: catKey, shape, label: '' };
      if (block) line.block = block;
      if (shape === SHAPES.QTY_RATE) {
        line.qty = 1;
        line.qtyUnit = categoryFixedUnit(catKey) ?? '';
        /* A vehicle's rate starts empty so the type can prefill it. */
        line.rate = catKey === 'vehicles' ? null : 0;
      }
      if (shape === SHAPES.LUMP) {
        line.amount = 0;
        if (catKey === 'subcontracts') line.sheet = 'new'; else line.desc = '';
      }
      if (catKey === 'personnel-salary') {
        /* Untitled on purpose — the row opens with its title empty and says so. */
        Object.assign(line, { qty: 1, staff: 1, timeUnit: 'month', qtyUnit: 'months' });
      }
      if (catKey === 'travel') applyTravelKind(line, kind || 'lodging');
      if (catKey === 'vehicles' && kind) applyVehicleKind(line, kind);
      if ((catKey === 'meetings' || catKey === 'other') && kind && shape === SHAPES.QTY_RATE) applyCostKind(line, kind);
      syncLabel(line);

      lines.push(line);
      const tr = mountRow(line);
      if (!tr) { lines.pop(); return; }
      tr.classList.add('is-added');
      window.setTimeout(() => tr.classList.remove('is-added'), 1500);
      commitEdit();
      unfoldTo(tr);
      tr.scrollIntoView({ block: 'nearest', behavior: 'smooth' });
      window.requestAnimationFrame(() => {
        /* The first question: where it goes, for travel; its name, elsewhere. */
        const first: any = catKey === 'travel' ? $('[data-field="destination"]', tr)
          : catKey === 'vehicles' ? null : $('[data-field="label"]', tr);
        first?.shadowRoot?.querySelector('input')?.focus();
      });
    };

    /* ── Add-line menus: the vendor's vocabulary, not the model's ── */
    const SHAPE_MENU_LABEL: Record<string, string> = {
      [SHAPES.QTY_RATE]: 'item, a quantity × cost each',
      [SHAPES.LUMP]: 'lump sum, one amount',
    };
    $$('[data-add-menu]').forEach((menu: any) => {
      const cat: any = categories.find((c: any) => c.key === menu.dataset.addMenu);
      if (!cat) return;
      if (cat.kinds) {
        menu.items = cat.kinds.flatMap((k: any) => [
          ...(k.vendorDefined ? [{ divider: true }] : []),
          { label: k.vendorDefined ? `${k.label} — describe your own` : k.label, action: `${cat.key}||${SHAPES.QTY_RATE}|${k.key}` },
        ]);
        if (cat.shapes.includes(SHAPES.LUMP)) {
          menu.items = [...menu.items, { divider: true }, { label: 'Lump sum — one amount', action: `${cat.key}||${SHAPES.LUMP}|` }];
        }
        return;
      }
      const blocks = cat.blocks ?? [null];
      menu.items = blocks.flatMap((b: any, bi: number) => [
        ...(bi > 0 ? [{ divider: true }] : []),
        ...cat.shapes.map((s: string) => ({
          label: b ? `${b.label} — ${SHAPE_MENU_LABEL[s]}` : SHAPE_MENU_LABEL[s],
          action: `${cat.key}|${b ? b.key : ''}|${s}|`,
        })),
      ]);
    });

    /* ── The one section setting: the budget's default fringe rate ── */
    const wireCatMenus = () => {
      $$('[data-cat-menu]').forEach((m: any) => {
        m.items = [{ label: `Adjust default fringe (${V.fringeDefaultText()}%)…`, action: 'cat|fringe' }];
      });
    };
    wireCatMenus();
    const fringeDialog: any = document.querySelector('[data-fringe-dialog]');
    const openFringeDialog = () => {
      if (!fringeDialog) return;
      const f: any = fringeDialog.querySelector('[data-fringe-default-field]');
      const own = lines.filter((l) => isFringeOverride(l)).length;
      f.value = V.fringeDefaultText();
      f.helpText = own
        ? `Applies to every position without its own rate. ${own} ${own === 1 ? 'line keeps its' : 'lines keep their'} own.`
        : 'Applies to every position without its own rate.';
      fringeDialog.show();
      window.requestAnimationFrame(() => f?.shadowRoot?.querySelector('input')?.focus());
    };
    fringeDialog?.addEventListener('click', (e: any) => {
      const t = e.target as HTMLElement;
      if (t.closest('[data-fringe-cancel]')) { fringeDialog.close(); return; }
      if (!t.closest('[data-fringe-save]')) return;
      fringeDefaults.pct = Math.max(0, num(fringeDialog.querySelector('[data-fringe-default-field]')?.value)) / 100;
      /* A line with its own rate does not move — that is what overriding means. */
      const following = lines.filter((l) => isSalaryLine(l) && !isFringeOverride(l));
      following.forEach((l) => { const tr = rowOf(l.id); if (tr) fillRow(tr, l); });
      fringeDialog.close();
      commitEdit();
      flash(following.map((l) => rowOf(l.id)));
      wireCatMenus();
    });

    /* ── Every action a row can take, in one place ── */
    function runRowAction(act: string, line: any, tr: HTMLElement) {
      if (!canEdit()) return;
      if (act === 'delete') {
        if (V.derivedRow(line)) return;
        const i = lines.findIndex((l) => l.id === line.id);
        if (i >= 0) lines.splice(i, 1);
        tr.remove();
        commitEdit();
        return;
      }
      /* Linked quantity: one hop, from the menu, both directions the vendor's. */
      if (act.startsWith('link|')) {
        linkQtyTo(line, act.slice(5));
        fillRow(tr, line);
        commitEdit(act.slice(5));
        flash([tr]);
        return;
      }
      if (act === 'detach-qty') { detachQty(line, lines); fillRow(tr, line); commitEdit(); flash([tr]); return; }
      if (act === 'refollow-qty') { refollowQty(line); fillRow(tr, line); commitEdit(); flash([tr]); return; }
      /* Supplies are filed by hand: the row moves to the other class's block. */
      if (act === 'move-class') {
        line.block = V.otherClassOf(line);
        tr.dataset.block = line.block;
        insertRow(tr, line);
        commitEdit();
        unfoldTo(tr);
        tr.scrollIntoView({ block: 'nearest', behavior: 'smooth' });
        flash([tr]);
        return;
      }
      if (act === 'fringe-override') {
        line.fringePct = fringeDefaults.pct;
        fillRow(tr, line);
        commitEdit(line.id);
        window.requestAnimationFrame(() => ($('[data-field="fringePct"]', tr) as any)?.shadowRoot?.querySelector('input')?.focus());
        return;
      }
      if (act === 'fringe-reset') {
        delete line.fringePct;
        fillRow(tr, line);
        commitEdit(line.id);
      }
    }

    root.addEventListener('menu-action', (e: any) => {
      const detail = String(e.detail ?? '');
      if (detail === 'cat|fringe') { if (canEdit()) openFringeDialog(); return; }
      if (detail.startsWith('row|')) {
        const tr = (e.target as HTMLElement)?.closest?.('tr[data-line]') as HTMLElement | null;
        const line = tr ? lineById(tr.dataset.line!) : null;
        if (tr && line) runRowAction(detail.slice(4), line, tr);
        return;
      }
      const [catKey, block, shape, kind] = detail.split('|');
      if (catKey && shape) addLine(catKey, block, shape, kind ?? '');
    });

    /* ── Every esa-* control fires a composed `change` — on blur for a text
       field, on pick for a select. That is the per-line autosave moment. ── */
    root.addEventListener('change', (e: any) => {
      const el = e.target as HTMLElement;
      const tr = el.closest?.('tr[data-line]') as HTMLElement | null;
      const line = tr ? lineById(tr.dataset.line!) : null;
      if (!tr || !line) return;
      const d = el.dataset as any;
      const value = (el as any).value;

      /* The vendor's tick on a mark — a review change, not a budget edit. */
      if ('markAddress' in d) {
        if (role() !== 'vendor' || !vendorCanEdit(review)) return;
        commitReview(setAddressed(review, line.id, !!(el as any).checked));
        return;
      }
      if (!canEdit()) return;

      if ('travelKindSelect' in d) { applyTravelKind(line, value); fillRow(tr, line); commitEdit(line.id); return; }
      if ('vehicleKindSelect' in d) { applyVehicleKind(line, value); fillRow(tr, line); commitEdit(line.id); return; }
      if ('vehicleTypeSelect' in d) {
        const prev = { vehicleKind: line.vehicleKind, vehicleType: line.vehicleType };
        line.vehicleType = String(value ?? '') || undefined;
        prefillVehicleRate(line, prev);
        syncLabel(line);
        fillRow(tr, line);
        commitEdit(line.id);
        flash([tr]);
        return;
      }
      if ('meetingKindSelect' in d || 'otherKindSelect' in d) { applyCostKind(line, value); fillRow(tr, line); commitEdit(line.id); return; }
      if ('timeUnitSelect' in d) {
        line.timeUnit = value;
        line.qtyUnit = timeUnit(line).plural;
        commitEdit(line.id);
        return;
      }

      const field = d.field;
      if (!field) return;
      if (field === 'label' || field === 'qtyUnit' || field === 'qty2Unit') line[field] = String(value ?? '');
      else if (field === 'destination' || field === 'desc') { line[field] = String(value ?? '').trim(); syncLabel(line); }
      else if (field === 'staff') line.staff = Math.max(1, Math.round(num(value) || 1));
      else if (field === 'fringePct') line.fringePct = num(value) / 100;
      else line[field] = num(value);
      commitEdit(line.id);
    });

    /* ── Clicks: fold, add, and the subcontract seam ── */
    root.addEventListener('click', (e: any) => {
      const t = e.target as HTMLElement;
      const toggle = t.closest?.('[data-cat-toggle]');
      if (toggle) {
        const tb = toggle.closest('tbody[data-cat]') as HTMLElement | null;
        setFolded(tb, !tb?.hasAttribute('data-collapsed'));
        return;
      }
      if (t.closest?.('[data-fold-all]')) { $$('tbody[data-cat]').forEach((tb) => setFolded(tb, true, false)); writeOpen(); return; }
      if (t.closest?.('[data-unfold-all]')) { $$('tbody[data-cat]').forEach((tb) => setFolded(tb, false, false)); writeOpen(); return; }
      const add = t.closest?.('[data-add-line]') as HTMLElement | null;
      if (add) {
        const [catKey, block, shape, kind] = String(add.dataset.addLine).split('|');
        addLine(catKey, block, shape, kind ?? '');
        return;
      }
      const sheet = t.closest?.('[data-open-sheet]') as HTMLElement | null;
      if (sheet) window.location.href = withBase(`/lib-mvp/subcontract/${sheet.dataset.openSheet || 'new'}`);
    });

    /* ── Go to line ── */
    const focusLine = (lineId: string) => {
      let line = lineById(lineId);
      if (!line) return;
      /* The vendor never sees Personnel — fringe; its salary line stands in. */
      if (V.derivedRow(line) && role() === 'vendor') line = lineById(line.base?.lineId) ?? line;
      const tr = rowOf(line.id);
      if (!tr) return;
      unfoldTo(tr);
      tr.scrollIntoView({ block: 'center', behavior: 'smooth' });
      flash([tr]);
    };
    document.addEventListener(EVENTS.focusLine, (e: any) => {
      const { lineId, budget } = e.detail ?? {};
      if (!lineId || (budget && budget !== budgetId)) return;
      focusLine(lineId);
    });

    /* ── The overhead block owns the pick; this grid owns the base ── */
    document.addEventListener(EVENTS.indirect, (e: any) => {
      if (isSub) return;
      const incoming = e.detail?.config;
      if (!incoming) return;
      cfg = withResolvedIndirect({ ...subIndirectCfg(), rateId: incoming.rateId ?? null });
      recompute();
      flash($$('[data-indirect-row]'));
    });

    /* ── The review round trip — identity check first: this grid fires the
       same event, and repainting its own echo would be work for nothing. ── */
    document.addEventListener(EVENTS.review, (e: any) => {
      const incoming = e.detail?.review;
      if (!incoming || incoming === review) return;
      review = incoming;
      lines.forEach((l) => { const tr = rowOf(l.id); if (tr) fillMarkForm(tr, l); });
      paintReview();
      paintPermissions();
      recompute();
    });
    document.addEventListener('cbf-role:change', () => { paintPermissions(); paintReview(); paintEmpty(); });

    /* ── Mount ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
       A stored or cleared budget differs from what the server rendered, so its
       rows are rebuilt from the working copy (in list order, each into its own
       section and block). Otherwise the server's rows stand and are seeded. */
    if (stored || blank) {
      $$('tr[data-line]').forEach((tr) => tr.remove());
      lines.forEach((l) => mountRow(l));
    } else {
      lines.forEach((l) => { const tr = rowOf(l.id); if (tr) { fillRow(tr, l); fillMarkForm(tr, l); } });
      $$('tr[data-line]').forEach(wireRow);
    }
    fringeSig = lines.filter((l) => l.category === 'personnel-fringe').map((l) => l.id).join('|');
    paintPermissions();
    paintReview();
    recompute();
    /* A first-run budget opens every section, so there is somewhere to add. */
    if (!lines.length) $$('tbody[data-cat]').forEach((tb) => setFolded(tb, false, false));

    /* A link to a line — `#<lineId>` (or `#line=<lineId>`) — lands on it. */
    const hash = decodeURIComponent(location.hash.replace(/^#(line=)?/, ''));
    if (hash) window.requestAnimationFrame(() => focusLine(hash));

    /* Re-broadcast on load so a sibling whose script initialises after this one
       still gets the state (a pure snapshot, so repeating it is harmless). */
    const rebroadcast = () => fireTotals(priceLines(lines, cfg).totals);
    if (document.readyState === 'complete') window.setTimeout(rebroadcast, 0);
    else window.addEventListener('load', rebroadcast, { once: true });
  }
</script>

<style>
  /* Dense entry surface: 14px table base, 13px for the quiet second lines — and
     DARKENED as it shrinks (text-secondary, never a muted gray). The literal
     sizes are deliberate: the --type-size-* clamps bottom out under the 13px
     floor on narrow viewports. */
  .cbf-lct__lede {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--color-content-default-secondary);
  }
  .cbf-lct__sr {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip-path: inset(50%);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .cbf-lct__saved {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--color-content-default-secondary);
  }

  /* overflow stays VISIBLE so the popovers and menus can escape; horizontal
     scroll is the last resort at genuinely narrow widths. */
  .cbf-lct__scroll {
    overflow: visible;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-default);
    border-radius: var(--radius-200);
    background: var(--color-background-elevation-raised);
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .cbf-lct__scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  }
  .cbf-lct__table {
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 900px;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--color-content-default);
  }

  /* ── Per-category column captions — quieter than a table head, because they
     repeat nine times and must read as captions, not as nine tables. ── */
  .cbf-lct__colhead th {
    text-align: left;
    padding: var(--spacing-150) var(--spacing-300);
    background: var(--color-background-elevation-raised);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-default);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: var(--typography-font-weight-semibold);
    color: var(--color-content-default-secondary);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .cbf-lct__colhead .cbf-lct__col-num { text-align: right; }
  .cbf-lct__col-span { min-width: 380px; }
  .cbf-lct__col-line { min-width: 250px; }
  /* Holds the whole multiplication on one line: two numbers, two units, the ×. */
  .cbf-lct__col-qty { min-width: 300px; }
  .cbf-lct__col-rate { min-width: 180px; }
  .cbf-lct__col-fringe { min-width: 180px; }
  .cbf-lct__col-act { width: 44px; }
  .cbf-lct__col-num { text-align: right; min-width: 115px; }

  .cbf-lct__cell {
    padding: var(--spacing-150) var(--spacing-250);
    vertical-align: top;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-default-subtle);
  }
  .cbf-lct__cell--num {
    text-align: right;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .cbf-lct__cell--act { text-align: right; }
  .cbf-lct__cell--void { color: var(--color-content-default-secondary); }

  /* ── Category + sub-block heads ── */
  .cbf-lct__cathead th {
    text-align: left;
    padding: var(--spacing-300);
    background: var(--cbf-surface-section-head, var(--color-background-elevation-sunken));
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-default-strong);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-default);
    font-weight: var(--typography-font-weight-regular);
  }
  .cbf-lct__cathead .cbf-lct__cell {
    background: var(--cbf-surface-section-head, var(--color-background-elevation-sunken));
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-default-strong);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-default);
    vertical-align: middle;
  }
  /* ── Folding — a folded section keeps only its head. ── */
  tbody[data-collapsed] > tr:not(.cbf-lct__cathead) { display: none; }
  [data-cat-toggle] :global(esa-icon),
  [data-cat-toggle] :global(svg) { transition: transform 150ms ease; }
  tbody[data-collapsed] [data-cat-toggle] :global(esa-icon),
  tbody[data-collapsed] [data-cat-toggle] :global(svg) { transform: rotate(-90deg); }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    [data-cat-toggle] :global(esa-icon),
    [data-cat-toggle] :global(svg) { transition: none; }
  }

  /* ── Row controls on hover; always visible on touch ── */
  @media (hover: hover) {
    .cbf-lct__hover { opacity: 0; transition: opacity 120ms ease; }
    tr:hover .cbf-lct__hover,
    tr:focus-within .cbf-lct__hover,
    .cbf-lct__hover:has([aria-expanded='true']),
    .cbf-lct__hover:focus-within { opacity: 1; }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .cbf-lct__hover { transition: none; }
  }

  .cbf-lct__cat-note {
    display: block;
    width: 22rem;
    max-width: 80vw;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--color-content-default);
  }
  .cbf-lct__cat-icon {
    display: inline-flex;
    color: var(--color-content-default-secondary);
  }
  .cbf-lct__cat-label {
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: var(--typography-font-weight-semibold);
    color: var(--color-content-default);
  }
  .cbf-lct__blockhead th {
    text-align: left;
    padding: var(--spacing-200) var(--spacing-300) var(--spacing-200) var(--spacing-500);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-default);
    font-weight: var(--typography-font-weight-regular);
  }
  .cbf-lct__blockhead .cbf-lct__cell {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-default);
    vertical-align: middle;
  }
  .cbf-lct__block-label {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: var(--typography-font-weight-semibold);
    color: var(--color-content-default);
  }

  /* ── Quiet second lines ── */
  .cbf-lct__note {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--color-content-default-secondary);
    max-width: 46ch;
  }
  .cbf-lct__void-mark {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--color-content-default-secondary);
    line-height: 40px;
  }
  /* A value the vendor did NOT type — derived. Reads as a value, never as a
     disabled control. */
  .cbf-lct__ref,
  .cbf-lct__derived {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: var(--typography-font-weight-medium);
    color: var(--color-content-default);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .cbf-lct__derived { font-weight: var(--typography-font-weight-regular); }
  .cbf-lct__qty-chain {
    --align: center;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .cbf-lct__times {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--color-content-default-secondary);
    align-self: center;
  }

  /* ── Entry controls ── */
  .cbf-lct__field--label { width: 100%; }
  .cbf-lct__field--qty { width: 64px; }
  .cbf-lct__field--unit { width: 80px; }
  .cbf-lct__field--staff { width: 52px; }
  .cbf-lct__field--rate { width: 104px; }
  /* Fits "$ 4,750 /month" whole — both affixes eat into the box. */
  .cbf-lct__field--rate-unit { width: 168px; }
  .cbf-lct__field--pct { width: 84px; }
  .cbf-lct__field--amount { width: 116px; margin-inline-start: auto; }
  .cbf-lct__select { width: 100%; }
  .cbf-lct__select--unit { width: 104px; }
  .cbf-lct__dialog-actions { justify-content: flex-end; }
  .cbf-lct__unit {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--color-content-default-secondary);
    align-self: center;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  /* Rate and the dollars it generates read as one phrase. */
  .cbf-lct__cell--fringe [data-fringe] { flex-wrap: nowrap; white-space: nowrap; }

  .cbf-lct__money {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    font-weight: var(--typography-font-weight-semibold);
  }

  /* Until esa-popover upgrades, every child renders inline — including the mark
     form. Keep the panels closed until hydration (or if it never comes). */
  esa-popover:not(:defined) [slot='content'] { display: none; }

  /* ── Line rows: a subtle divider between each, a tint on hover. The first
     row's divider collapses into the column-header rule above it. ── */
  tr[data-line] > .cbf-lct__cell { border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-default-subtle); }
  @media (hover: hover) {
    tr[data-line]:hover > .cbf-lct__cell {
      background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-content-default) 3%, transparent);
    }
  }
  /* ── Row state: an inline background tint, NEVER a colored left border ── */
  tr[data-flag='months'] > .cbf-lct__cell { background: var(--color-background-utility-danger-subtle); }
  tr[data-flag='error'] > .cbf-lct__cell { background: var(--color-background-utility-warning-subtle); }

